{
  "summary": "Ensure all initial outbound connections (default 3) for private transaction broadcast complete even if the transaction is received back from the network or conflicted before completion. Replace immediate transaction removal upon network receipt with a resolved flag, preventing additional retry connections via TryGrantRetry while allowing pending initial sends to finish. Remove DidNodeConfirmReception in favor of checking whether the connection completed its handshake before scheduling compensation attempts.",
  "problem": "When a privately broadcast transaction was received back from the network or became invalid in the mempool before all initial connections finished, the node immediately removed the transaction and canceled any remaining unestablished connections. This introduced a timing side channel where adversaries returning a transaction quickly could suppress remaining outbound connections and correlate broadcasts.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Intended as an alternative to #34707, addressing the theoretical timing attack described in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34707#issuecomment-5603256702. Also fixes theoretical timing attacks described in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29415#discussion_r2035693786.'"
